schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Decentralization and Resilience
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: framework
  summary: >-
    Frames decentralization as a practical foundation for community survival
    rather than a technical abstraction, via four mechanisms — redundancy,
    fault tolerance, adaptive capacity, and anti-fragility — then introduces
    "cosmo-local coordination" (global standards + local control) and gives
    regenerative-community applications (local ReFi nodes, decentralized
    energy/food networks, community savings circles/ROSCAs) plus six
    principles for building resilient regeneration.
  audience: Community-Steward
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      local-autonomy vs global-coordination — "isolation breeds fragility;
      dependence on a single external power breeds capture."
  related_concepts:
    - cosmo-local-coordination
    - anti-fragility
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/decentralization-resilience.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-b48196973cdf
  source_lineage: decentralization-resilience.md
  notes: >
    # assessed-but-excluded

    - Greenpill Local and RadicalxChange appear only in the reference list
      (URLs, no in-body description of what they curate or a return path), so
      no source-system card was created for either here — insufficient
      in-article material to responsibly fill steward/return_path without
      inventing facts.
    - ROSCA (rotating savings and loan association) is described only generically
      as "a time-tested form of decentralization"; not enough distinct source
      material for its own concept-lineage beyond what's captured in the
      encyclopedia entry's applications section.
    - No people/community profiles, exact locations, or high-risk triggers
      identified; no public-use-boundary object created.
